From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 02:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clk: cix: register Sky1 ACPI CLKT clkdev bridge at core_initcall

On Sky1 with ACPI (acpi=force) there are no DT "clocks" phandles; the
clk-sky1-acpi CLKT bridge (patch 0096) synthesizes clkdev aliases from the
firmware CLKT packages, mapping each consumer name to its scmi-clk-<id>.
Registered with module_platform_driver() the bridge runs at module_init,
AFTER built-in VPU (amvx), display (linlondp), pwm-sky1, usb3-phy and audss
consumers have already probed. Those consumers get -ENOENT (audss converts it
to a NULL parent) and are never retried, so vpu_clk / engine clk / apb clocks
resolve to nothing and the devices fail (VPU probe hard-faults / graceful clk
failure; display/pwm/phy dead) even though SCMI has published the clocks.

Register the platform driver at core_initcall so the aliases exist before the
consumers probe. Safe to precede the ACPI device or SCMI: device/driver
matching handles the former and the probe's existing -EPROBE_DEFER handles the
latter.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c b/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
index 4c5ca954da00..3b75a2ea0f03 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
@@ -193,7 +193,22 @@ static struct platform_driver sky1_acpi_clk_driver = {
 	},
 	.probe = sky1_acpi_clk_probe,
 };
-module_platform_driver(sky1_acpi_clk_driver);
+
+static int __init sky1_acpi_clk_init(void)
+{
+	if (acpi_disabled)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	return platform_driver_register(&sky1_acpi_clk_driver);
+}
+core_initcall(sky1_acpi_clk_init);
+
+/* CIX_ACPI_CLK is bool; retain a teardown path for completeness/testing. */
+static void __exit sky1_acpi_clk_exit(void)
+{
+	platform_driver_unregister(&sky1_acpi_clk_driver);
+}
+module_exit(sky1_acpi_clk_exit);
 
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("CIX Sky1 ACPI clock lookup table driver");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
-- 
